      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Zebulon lies within the Upper Flint River sub‑basin, where the Flint River begins near Atlanta and feeds southern agricultural lands.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Zebulon,_Georgia",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "By the early 1900s, cotton booms in Pike County spurred railroads linking Zebulon to Atlanta, boosting local prosperity.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
